Q: monitor_window_timeout using msal-browser A: <p>The best way to debug why your iframe is timing out is to go find it in your DOM and make it visible on the screen, so you can see what's it's doing.</p>
<p>Set you msalConfig to have a really long <code>iframeBridgeTimout</code> value:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>export const msalConfig: Configuration = {
  auth: {
    clientId: config.azure.clientId,
    authority: `https://login.microsoftonline.com/${config.azure.tenantId}`,
    redirectUri: window.location.origin + &quot;/auth/callback&quot;
    postLogoutRedirectUri: &quot;/&quot;,
  },
  system: {
    iframeBridgeTimeout: 60000, //one minute
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Then retrigger your <code>silentsso</code> or <code>acquireTokenSilent</code> call.</p>
<p>Open your browser dev tools and find the iframe at the bottom of the DOM.</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;html&gt;
   &lt;body&gt;
   ...your site
   &lt;iframe class=&quot;msalSilentIframe&quot; style=&quot;visibility: hidden; position: absolute; height: 0px; width: 0px; border: 0px;&quot; ...&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;
   &lt;/body
&lt;/html&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Delete the entire <code>style</code> html property right in the browser tools, which will get rid of the styling that's hiding it from your screen.</p>
<p>Go back to your browser and you should be able to see the iframe and what it's stuck on.</p>
<p>For me, my iframe was blocked because of recent Edge security features blocking iframes that redirect to a private network.</p>
<p><a href="https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-js/issues/8100" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-js/issues/8100</a></p>
<p>Another issue is if you aren't calling <code>broadcastResponseToMainFrame()</code> on your callback page.
<a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/msal/javascript/browser/v4-migration#1-set-up-the-redirect-bridge-page" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/msal/javascript/browser/v4-migration#1-set-up-the-redirect-bridge-page</a></p>
